# The retained axial coefficient can change the next finite resonant row

This explicit degree-13 sensitivity polynomial is extracted from the exact linearized
Cartesian source recurrence. Its coefficients are fixed in this owner. The kernel proves it
positive throughout the prior amplitude-root interval. Attachment to C28[z^4] and the complete
constant forcing of that row retain their separately declared computational/open scopes.
-/

noncomputable section

